        "id": "ch4_3_1-1",
        "text": "Booleans\nA Boolean-type variable can hold one of two values; true or false. That\u2019s it. It\u2019s called a System.\nBoolean or [bool] . [bool] is an accelerator and saves us from having to type a much longer\nclass name; it\u2019s an alias for the type System.Boolean . Booleans are easy to assign; we use the\nautomatic variables $True and $False . Try the following:\n$MyBoolean = $True\n$MyBoolean | Get-Member\nWe can see that the type is System.Boolean . Variables with this type are useful in scripting, as\nwe will see in Chapter 5 , PowerShell Control Flow \u2013 Conditionals and Loops . In that chapter, we\u2019ll also\nsee a similar but subtly different value type, the [switch] type \u2013 that can also only be true or false\nbut has a different set of members.\nDiscovering value types\n87",
